\[\mathbf{A} - 2 \mathbf{I} =
\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
- 2
\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 3 \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}
.\]Then
\[\mathbf{A} (\mathbf{A} - 2 \mathbf{I}) =
\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 3 \\ 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 3 \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}
=
